# The upper-form files this module keeps but does not build.
#
# Nothing, as of 6 September 2026, and the four that used to be here are the
# reason the file still exists rather than a reason to keep it.
#
# They were held out because building them would put our bytecode where IBM's
# is and give up the byte identity English was checked by. That property was
# retired: the gate is test/matrix.sh and test/words.sh, which hold this
# engine to what this engine said before, and neither cares whose bytecode it
# is. Holding rules out of the build to protect a claim nothing was checking
# any more only meant English's rules could not be edited, which is the one
# thing the compiler was written for.
#
# tools/rules/check-upper.sh is unaffected and still runs: it builds both
# sides itself, the lifted text alone against the same with every upper-form
# file compiled in, whatever this file says. What it proves has changed name
# rather than substance -- that the compiler renders a rule faithfully, not
# that our bytecode is IBM's.
#
# What the file is for now is a rule being written: name it here while it is
# half done and the build will leave it alone.
